1
00:00:02,420 --> 00:00:03,670
Tsubasa.

2
00:00:05,090 --> 00:00:07,420
There's something I've always wanted to tell you.

3
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:09,380
Thank you.

4
00:00:09,880 --> 00:00:14,930
Being able to come this far is entirely thanks to you.

5
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:22,100
My football dream came true a long time ago.

6
00:00:23,310 --> 00:00:24,690
Ishizaki.

7
00:00:25,110 --> 00:00:28,440
But Tsubasa, please.

8
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:34,120
My dream now is for you to become the best footballer in the world.

9
00:00:35,620 --> 00:00:39,080
Don't let me down. Okay, Tsubasa?

10
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:41,410
What are you saying, Ishizaki?

11
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:45,710
This isn't just my dream, it's everyone's dream.

12
00:00:48,550 --> 00:00:50,170
That's right.

13
00:00:51,420 --> 00:00:55,430
But for me, it ends here.

14
00:00:57,060 --> 00:00:58,060
Ishizaki!

15
00:00:58,140 --> 00:00:59,770
- Ishizaki.
- Ishizaki!

16
00:00:59,850 --> 00:01:01,520
Hang in there, Ishizaki.

17
00:01:02,020 --> 00:01:03,190
Coach Sumitomo!

18
00:01:03,270 --> 00:01:04,650
Take Ishizaki to the infirmary!

19
00:01:04,940 --> 00:01:05,860
Yes, Head Coach.

20
00:01:05,940 --> 00:01:07,400
Izawa, you're on.

21
00:01:07,730 --> 00:01:08,650
Yes.

22
00:01:10,860 --> 00:01:13,490
Ishizaki is carried off on a stretcher.

23
00:01:13,570 --> 00:01:15,660
We are all worried about him.

24
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:17,410
Ryo.

25
00:01:17,580 --> 00:01:20,700
I'm sure Ishizaki will recover.

26
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:25,120
Japan sends Izawa on for Ishizaki.

27
00:01:26,540 --> 00:01:28,840
Goalkeeper: Wakabayashi

28
00:01:26,790 --> 00:01:31,420
7 minutes left in the match, and we're back to square one.

29
00:01:28,920 --> 00:01:31,590
Defender: Matsuyama

30
00:01:28,920 --> 00:01:31,590
Defender: Soda

31
00:01:28,920 --> 00:01:31,590
Defender: Jito

32
00:01:31,670 --> 00:01:33,840
Midfielder: Sawada

33
00:01:31,670 --> 00:01:33,840
Midfielder: Sano

34
00:01:31,960 --> 00:01:36,340
Which team will score the winning goal?

35
00:01:33,930 --> 00:01:36,340
Midfielder: Tsubasa

36
00:01:33,930 --> 00:01:36,340
Midfielder: Misaki

37
00:01:36,430 --> 00:01:39,350
Forward: Hyuga

38
00:01:36,430 --> 00:01:39,350
Forward: Nitta

39
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:39,350
No one can predict.

40
00:01:39,430 --> 00:01:41,850
Midfielder: Schester

41
00:01:39,430 --> 00:01:41,850
Forward: Margas

42
00:01:39,430 --> 00:01:41,850
Forward: Schneider

43
00:01:41,930 --> 00:01:44,850
Defensive Midfielder: Max

44
00:01:41,930 --> 00:01:44,850
Defensive Midfielder: Kaltz

45
00:01:42,680 --> 00:01:44,850
Right now, it's about mental strength.

46
00:01:44,940 --> 00:01:47,610
Defender: Hein

47
00:01:44,940 --> 00:01:47,610
Defender: Mayer

48
00:01:44,940 --> 00:01:47,610
Defender: Magath

49
00:01:44,940 --> 00:01:47,610
Defender: Mylus

50
00:01:44,940 --> 00:01:47,610
Defender: Hardwich

51
00:01:45,310 --> 00:01:47,610
This is Japanese spirit versus German spirit.

52
00:01:47,690 --> 00:01:49,940
Goalkeeper: Müller

53
00:01:47,900 --> 00:01:51,900
As representatives of Germany, we can't lose to Japan!

54
00:01:51,980 --> 00:01:53,190
Right!

55
00:01:53,950 --> 00:01:57,160
Guys, don't forget Ishizaki's courage.

56
00:01:57,570 --> 00:02:02,750
He may not be on the field, but his spirit is in our hearts.

57
00:02:03,410 --> 00:02:05,870
The match is tied, and we start from here.

58
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:09,290
We will be the ones to score the winning goal.

59
00:02:09,380 --> 00:02:10,750
Yes!

60
00:02:23,350 --> 00:02:28,270
CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC

61
00:03:42,500 --> 00:03:48,460
Episode 35
It's Over!

62
00:03:43,290 --> 00:03:46,630
This is the final of the first National Youth Tournament in France.

63
00:03:46,710 --> 00:03:48,460
It's finally coming to an end.

64
00:03:48,550 --> 00:03:52,010
The score is 2-2, and only 7 minutes remain.

65
00:03:52,260 --> 00:03:56,890
Both teams have displayed fast-paced play from the start.

66
00:03:57,310 --> 00:04:00,140
They are undoubtedly extremely tired.

67
00:04:00,430 --> 00:04:05,190
But this hasn't affected their speed and movement.

68
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:08,150
This shows their high mental strength.

69
00:04:08,860 --> 00:04:10,900
Both desperately want this victory.

70
00:04:11,110 --> 00:04:15,660
Who will score the winning goal? Japan or Germany?

71
00:04:17,580 --> 00:04:20,290
Now Japan starts the play.

72
00:04:20,580 --> 00:04:21,910
We won't lose!

73
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:25,540
We'll give our all for Ishizaki.

74
00:04:25,880 --> 00:04:26,750
This victory is ours!

75
00:04:26,830 --> 00:04:29,800
Victory belongs to Germany!

76
00:04:30,340 --> 00:04:34,340
One more goal will give me a hat-trick in every match, and then I...

77
00:04:34,430 --> 00:04:36,550
will make Germany the world champion.

78
00:04:36,930 --> 00:04:42,230
Going into extra time would be a disadvantage for us.

79
00:04:42,310 --> 00:04:44,140
Let's finish it in these 7 minutes.

80
00:04:44,230 --> 00:04:46,600
Guys, give it your last effort.

81
00:04:46,730 --> 00:04:49,570
Japan will win.

82
00:04:50,900 --> 00:04:52,320
The ball has come loose!

83
00:04:52,650 --> 00:04:55,070
The two captains are after the ball!

84
00:04:55,150 --> 00:04:56,820
- Tsubasa!
- Schneider!

85
00:04:58,910 --> 00:05:00,950
Another clash of the great rivals!

86
00:05:01,740 --> 00:05:04,830
Schneider, using both feet, wins it!

87
00:05:05,250 --> 00:05:06,210
Tsubasa!

88
00:05:07,130 --> 00:05:08,210
Alright, let's go.

89
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:10,710
Damn.

90
00:05:11,050 --> 00:05:14,470
Schneider attacks directly toward Japan's goal.

91
00:05:14,760 --> 00:05:16,380
Come on, Schneider.

92
00:05:16,470 --> 00:05:18,970
Even if I die, I won't let you score the winning goal.

93
00:05:19,260 --> 00:05:21,010
Get ready, Wakabayashi.

94
00:05:21,180 --> 00:05:24,350
I tricked you on the second goal, but this time...

95
00:05:24,480 --> 00:05:26,190
No tricks.

96
00:05:26,520 --> 00:05:29,110
This time I'll score face to face.

97
00:05:29,560 --> 00:05:31,730
He's preparing to shoot.

98
00:05:32,030 --> 00:05:33,480
I know Wakabayashi said...

99
00:05:33,570 --> 00:05:36,360
we can let Schneider shoot from outside the box, but...

100
00:05:36,450 --> 00:05:38,490
Now we'll prevent it.

101
00:05:38,780 --> 00:05:39,990
Fire!

102
00:05:40,410 --> 00:05:44,500
Schneider unleashes a Fire Shot with all his remaining strength!

103
00:05:44,580 --> 00:05:46,750
- Where?
- I can't see the ball.

104
00:05:47,040 --> 00:05:48,250
It's a goal.

105
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:50,210
He stopped it!

106
00:05:50,290 --> 00:05:53,920
He saves Schneider's extremely fast shot with a dive!

107
00:05:54,010 --> 00:05:57,760
Just what you'd expect from super goalkeeper Genzo Wakabayashi.

108
00:05:58,050 --> 00:06:00,390
Wakabayashi, you...

109
00:06:00,720 --> 00:06:03,140
- Great!
- Well done, Wakabayashi!

110
00:06:08,440 --> 00:06:09,900
Can you hear me?

111
00:06:09,980 --> 00:06:12,770
Coach Sumitomo, what happened in the match?

112
00:06:12,980 --> 00:06:16,320
Still tied. Less than 5 minutes left.

113
00:06:17,200 --> 00:06:18,400
You shouldn't get up yet.

114
00:06:19,030 --> 00:06:20,620
Please let me go.

115
00:06:20,950 --> 00:06:22,530
I have to watch.

116
00:06:22,910 --> 00:06:25,660
I may not be able to stand on the field...

117
00:06:26,290 --> 00:06:29,040
But I want to see the moment Tsubasa and the guys win.

118
00:06:29,330 --> 00:06:32,380
With my own eyes, I want to see that moment...

119
00:06:32,460 --> 00:06:34,420
The moment the dream we vowed together comes true.

120
00:06:34,800 --> 00:06:36,590
Just rest a little more.

121
00:06:36,670 --> 00:06:38,170
It's going into extra time now.

122
00:06:38,510 --> 00:06:40,890
No, he'll settle it in this half.

123
00:06:41,260 --> 00:06:45,560
I know Tsubasa will finish it. I can feel it.

124
00:06:45,720 --> 00:06:46,560
Here.

125
00:06:46,970 --> 00:06:49,940
Wakabayashi sends the ball with a tremendous long kick.

126
00:06:50,100 --> 00:06:52,520
It reaches Hyuga directly!

127
00:06:52,610 --> 00:06:55,190
A great opportunity arises for Japan.

128
00:06:55,270 --> 00:06:56,440
Great, Wakabayashi.

129
00:06:56,860 --> 00:06:57,690
No.

130
00:06:58,320 --> 00:07:02,700
The second goal proved I'm Japan's best forward.

131
00:07:04,030 --> 00:07:08,910
And this one will show I'm the world's best forward!

132
00:07:10,210 --> 00:07:14,340
Catch! New Tiger Shot!

133
00:07:14,790 --> 00:07:19,090
It's unleashed! This is Kojiro Hyuga's New Tiger Shot!

134
00:07:23,850 --> 00:07:27,140
Damn! My right arm, from the previous shot...

135
00:07:28,560 --> 00:07:32,230
Müller stops the ball on the right side with his left hand.

136
00:07:33,230 --> 00:07:37,980
Oh, but the power of Hyuga's shot knocks the ball out of his hand.

137
00:07:38,320 --> 00:07:39,990
No, now it's going to be a goal.

138
00:07:40,900 --> 00:07:41,740
Müller!

139
00:07:41,950 --> 00:07:43,070
No!

140
00:07:43,160 --> 00:07:44,820
The giant flies!

141
00:07:44,910 --> 00:07:48,750
Müller clears the ball with an overhead kick!

142
00:07:48,830 --> 00:07:49,660
What?

143
00:07:49,750 --> 00:07:51,000
Great, Müller.

144
00:07:51,410 --> 00:07:55,960
Japan has Wakabayashi, and Germany has Müller.

145
00:07:56,040 --> 00:07:59,800
Neither goalkeeper nor forwards are giving in.

146
00:07:59,880 --> 00:08:02,760
The two teams are completely equal.

147
00:08:03,220 --> 00:08:06,760
But Tsubasa gets the cleared ball.

148
00:08:07,140 --> 00:08:11,140
With 3 minutes left, will this be Japan's final attack?

149
00:08:11,230 --> 00:08:14,520
With Tsubasa, can they score the winning goal?

150
00:08:14,850 --> 00:08:16,400
Let's go, Tsubasa.

151
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:18,070
We trust you, Tsubasa.

152
00:08:18,150 --> 00:08:19,530
We support you.

153
00:08:19,820 --> 00:08:21,150
Alright, let's do this!

154
00:08:21,240 --> 00:08:25,110
The final dream goal will make our dream come true!

155
00:08:25,200 --> 00:08:27,780
Let's reach it together!

156
00:08:28,160 --> 00:08:30,290
Tsubasa starts dribbling.

157
00:08:30,500 --> 00:08:32,460
The Assist King.

158
00:08:32,540 --> 00:08:36,540
The man who contributed to every goal Japan scored in this tournament is attacking!

159
00:08:36,830 --> 00:08:41,550
Will Japan score the winning goal of this tournament?

160
00:08:41,760 --> 00:08:43,420
Go, Tsubasa!

161
00:08:43,760 --> 00:08:44,930
Tsubasa!

162
00:08:45,220 --> 00:08:46,260
We'll cut him off!

163
00:08:46,390 --> 00:08:47,180
Okay!

164
00:08:47,510 --> 00:08:53,480
He's stealing the championship of this tournament from us!

165
00:08:53,560 --> 00:08:57,150
It's thanks to him that we control the midfield.

166
00:08:58,150 --> 00:09:00,780
I'll stop his last move.

167
00:09:00,860 --> 00:09:04,450
We defenders will stop him before the situation gets worse.

168
00:09:04,740 --> 00:09:09,370
Roberto wrote, "If you control the midfield, you control the game."

169
00:09:09,450 --> 00:09:12,750
That's why I moved from forward to midfield.

170
00:09:12,910 --> 00:09:16,870
Will Japan score the winning goal?

171
00:09:17,130 --> 00:09:18,460
This is the final showdown.

172
00:09:18,540 --> 00:09:21,210
Tsubasa goes to pass the defense with dribbling.

173
00:09:21,630 --> 00:09:22,880
- Break him down!
- Shoot!

174
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:24,970
Germany tackles with all their might.

175
00:09:25,930 --> 00:09:28,340
Tsubasa jumps and evades.

176
00:09:28,930 --> 00:09:29,850
Great, Tsubasa.

177
00:09:32,930 --> 00:09:37,810
But the Knight of Bremen, Franz Schester, attacks him.

178
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:40,820
With a leap, he also passes Schester.

179
00:09:40,980 --> 00:09:42,070
I got you!

180
00:09:42,360 --> 00:09:43,570
Catch, here it comes!

181
00:09:44,740 --> 00:09:47,450
Kaltz had hidden behind Schester.

182
00:09:47,530 --> 00:09:51,330
And with a ruthless, fast tackle, he strikes Tsubasa.

183
00:09:51,450 --> 00:09:53,450
- Tsubasa!
- Great, Kaltz!

184
00:09:56,710 --> 00:09:57,540
Good!

185
00:09:57,620 --> 00:09:59,630
A great combination play from Germany.

186
00:09:59,710 --> 00:10:03,960
They take the ball from Tsubasa in midfield for the first time.

187
00:10:04,420 --> 00:10:07,340
This is our German spirit.

188
00:10:07,880 --> 00:10:08,970
Let's advance.

189
00:10:09,050 --> 00:10:09,970
Okay!

190
00:10:10,470 --> 00:10:11,680
Good luck, Germany!

191
00:10:11,760 --> 00:10:12,720
Win!

192
00:10:12,810 --> 00:10:17,230
Germany shows their resilience, and now they attack.

193
00:10:17,600 --> 00:10:20,610
The German youth, amid a flood of cheers from the fans...

194
00:10:20,690 --> 00:10:22,480
...attack Japan's goal.

195
00:10:22,770 --> 00:10:25,490
Oh, Tsubasa can't get up.

196
00:10:25,780 --> 00:10:26,740
Tsubasa.

197
00:10:28,110 --> 00:10:30,110
The game continues.

198
00:10:30,450 --> 00:10:31,740
Is he okay?

199
00:10:32,120 --> 00:10:34,410
Get up, Tsubasa!

200
00:10:34,490 --> 00:10:35,540
Ishizaki!

201
00:10:35,620 --> 00:10:39,870
If Tsubasa weren't injured, he would have passed them easily.

202
00:10:40,380 --> 00:10:44,500
His injury from the national championship still hasn't fully healed.

203
00:10:45,380 --> 00:10:47,010
It's obvious.

204
00:10:47,090 --> 00:10:50,220
It hasn't even been a month!

205
00:10:50,300 --> 00:10:52,760
But he played incredibly!

206
00:10:53,140 --> 00:10:56,520
Tsubasa is even more incredible at his best form.

207
00:10:56,770 --> 00:10:59,940
Please, Tsubasa, get up!

208
00:11:00,020 --> 00:11:03,980
You are the only one who can score the winning goal!

209
00:11:04,070 --> 00:11:07,940
We've been friends for a long time, I know you better than anyone.

210
00:11:08,030 --> 00:11:12,870
You are the only one who can make our dream come true.

211
00:11:13,740 --> 00:11:15,330
Ishizaki.

212
00:11:15,790 --> 00:11:16,910
I'll cut him off!

213
00:11:17,160 --> 00:11:18,160
Kaltz!

214
00:11:18,450 --> 00:11:20,790
Even though the Japanese players have turned to get the ball...

215
00:11:20,870 --> 00:11:23,920
The ball goes from Schester to the cunning Kaltz!

216
00:11:24,670 --> 00:11:27,960
You are the only one who can score.

217
00:11:28,050 --> 00:11:32,430
You are the future of Germany, no, of European football.

218
00:11:32,800 --> 00:11:34,600
You are Germany's Young Emperor...

219
00:11:34,680 --> 00:11:37,430
Karl Heinz Schneider!

220
00:11:37,520 --> 00:11:38,350
Okay.

221
00:11:38,430 --> 00:11:41,690
The final pass reaches Schneider in front of the goal.

222
00:11:43,230 --> 00:11:45,820
Less than 1 minute left.

223
00:11:45,900 --> 00:11:47,940
Is this the final shot?

224
00:11:48,280 --> 00:11:52,700
We, the German youth, are the winners of this match.

225
00:11:53,030 --> 00:11:55,580
- Cut him off!
- I'll block with my body!

226
00:11:58,200 --> 00:12:00,960
Schneider sends the ball into the air.

227
00:12:01,120 --> 00:12:01,960
What?

228
00:12:02,330 --> 00:12:04,920
He completely fooled them.

229
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:08,800
Despite everything, Schneider keeps his composure!

230
00:12:08,880 --> 00:12:12,590
He passes the defense and is now one-on-one with the goalkeeper.

231
00:12:12,680 --> 00:12:15,470
Wakabayashi can't come out!

232
00:12:15,890 --> 00:12:16,720
Wakabayashi!

233
00:12:17,180 --> 00:12:19,470
The cool-headed goal hunter Schneider...

234
00:12:19,560 --> 00:12:21,730
Unmarked, goes to shoot.

235
00:12:22,020 --> 00:12:23,230
Now or never.

236
00:12:24,520 --> 00:12:26,310
You moved too early, Wakabayashi.

237
00:12:26,520 --> 00:12:27,610
In this position...

238
00:12:27,690 --> 00:12:29,860
You have to pick a random side.

239
00:12:30,070 --> 00:12:34,240
But I saw where you were going from here!

240
00:12:34,570 --> 00:12:37,160
I figured it out. I'll shoot to the opposite corner!

241
00:12:37,700 --> 00:12:39,620
Another hat-trick on the way!

242
00:12:39,910 --> 00:12:43,040
And the winning goal for Germany!

243
00:12:47,710 --> 00:12:48,630
What!?

244
00:12:48,960 --> 00:12:53,880
Oh, this is Wakashimazu's special move, Sankaku Tobi!

245
00:12:53,970 --> 00:12:58,890
He moved left, but uses the post to leap to the right!

246
00:12:59,140 --> 00:13:02,390
But he's up high! The shot goes low!

247
00:13:02,730 --> 00:13:04,270
Wakabayashi!

248
00:13:05,650 --> 00:13:06,900
He stopped it!

249
00:13:06,980 --> 00:13:08,980
Germany couldn't score!

250
00:13:09,070 --> 00:13:13,150
Wakabayashi pushed off the crossbar and came down quickly and in time.

251
00:13:13,570 --> 00:13:14,400
Impossible!

252
00:13:15,410 --> 00:13:18,570
But even Wakabayashi couldn't catch it cleanly.

253
00:13:18,660 --> 00:13:19,660
He just stopped it.

254
00:13:19,990 --> 00:13:21,160
It still hasn't gone out of play.

255
00:13:21,410 --> 00:13:22,250
Good.

256
00:13:22,330 --> 00:13:24,910
Margas runs to strike the ball!

257
00:13:25,080 --> 00:13:26,040
I'll never allow it!

258
00:13:26,120 --> 00:13:28,080
He saved it!

259
00:13:28,170 --> 00:13:32,170
He defended Japan at the cost of his life. This is Genzo Wakabayashi!

260
00:13:32,340 --> 00:13:33,170
What!?

261
00:13:34,720 --> 00:13:36,380
Wakabayashi.

262
00:13:36,930 --> 00:13:39,930
I want to get up. I have to get up.

263
00:13:43,390 --> 00:13:44,930
Wakabayashi.

264
00:13:45,560 --> 00:13:46,390
Tsubasa!

265
00:13:46,480 --> 00:13:48,520
Come on, Wakabayashi!

266
00:13:48,600 --> 00:13:50,020
Tsubasa got up!

267
00:13:50,110 --> 00:13:51,360
Tsubasa!

268
00:13:51,440 --> 00:13:53,440
CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC

269
00:13:56,590 --> 00:13:58,930
Germany's defenders.

270
00:13:59,470 --> 00:14:01,470
Come, Wakabayashi!

271
00:14:01,840 --> 00:14:03,760
I was waiting for this, Tsubasa.

272
00:14:03,890 --> 00:14:05,680
I defended our goal.

273
00:14:05,770 --> 00:14:07,180
The rest is up to you.

274
00:14:07,430 --> 00:14:08,810
It's over, Wakabayashi.

275
00:14:08,940 --> 00:14:13,440
With the ball you stopped, I'll make us number one in the world.

276
00:14:14,440 --> 00:14:15,440
Tsubasa.

277
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:20,570
This cross will decide the fate of the battle.

278
00:14:26,660 --> 00:14:29,330
Three years have passed since my unforgettable first meeting with Tsubasa.

279
00:14:29,710 --> 00:14:33,580
You said you would go to Brazil and become a professional.

280
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:37,760
You inspired me, and I went to Germany.

281
00:14:38,340 --> 00:14:39,550
And now...

282
00:14:39,920 --> 00:14:44,300
We're fighting together for the world championship.

283
00:14:44,550 --> 00:14:48,470
That's right. Being number one is right in front of us.

284
00:14:49,350 --> 00:14:50,980
Oh, the sound of the whistle!

285
00:14:51,060 --> 00:14:53,560
Is it the end of the half? Or extra time?

286
00:14:53,810 --> 00:14:57,980
No, a foul was called on Margas for charging the goalkeeper.

287
00:14:58,070 --> 00:15:00,070
There's still time.

288
00:15:00,700 --> 00:15:02,070
Go forward, Tsubasa.

289
00:15:02,530 --> 00:15:03,950
No need for extra time!

290
00:15:04,200 --> 00:15:06,080
Let's settle this now.

291
00:15:06,530 --> 00:15:09,080
This is their last hopeful free kick!

292
00:15:09,370 --> 00:15:10,580
Your pass was great!

293
00:15:10,870 --> 00:15:12,170
It goes right to the center.

294
00:15:12,250 --> 00:15:17,090
And in the midfield, it's none other than captain Ozora Tsubasa.

295
00:15:17,380 --> 00:15:18,590
Let's go.

296
00:15:18,670 --> 00:15:20,590
Tsubasa starts dribbling.

297
00:15:20,670 --> 00:15:24,340
But two German defenders come to stop him.

298
00:15:24,640 --> 00:15:25,760
We'll break it up again!

299
00:15:25,850 --> 00:15:27,850
No scoring opportunity for you.

300
00:15:27,970 --> 00:15:29,350
What will Tsubasa choose?

301
00:15:29,430 --> 00:15:32,190
Without a doubt, he passed.

302
00:15:32,270 --> 00:15:33,100
What?

303
00:15:33,440 --> 00:15:35,480
I'm not the team's only midfielder.

304
00:15:35,560 --> 00:15:39,360
And I'm not the only playmaker here.

305
00:15:39,610 --> 00:15:42,860
The ball goes to the other midfielder, Misaki.

306
00:15:43,650 --> 00:15:45,740
I understand, Tsubasa.

307
00:15:46,160 --> 00:15:47,080
Let's go.

308
00:15:47,370 --> 00:15:51,370
Now the playmaker is Misaki, not Tsubasa.

309
00:15:51,450 --> 00:15:55,330
For the first time, and now, Misaki is dribbling.

310
00:15:55,460 --> 00:15:56,880
Go, Misaki!

311
00:15:56,960 --> 00:15:58,340
Misaki!

312
00:15:59,840 --> 00:16:02,090
Only a few moments remain.

313
00:16:02,340 --> 00:16:06,090
30 minutes have passed, only extra time remains.

314
00:16:06,180 --> 00:16:07,890
I won't let you pass.

315
00:16:08,640 --> 00:16:10,600
And he passes again.

316
00:16:11,930 --> 00:16:15,350
Misaki gets past with wonderful dribbling.

317
00:16:15,690 --> 00:16:16,940
Well done, Misaki!

318
00:16:17,020 --> 00:16:18,860
This is where Misaki shines.

319
00:16:19,110 --> 00:16:23,110
Incredible! His dribbling is just like number 10 Tsubasa.

320
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:27,120
Even in South America, his great performance would cause astonishment.

321
00:16:27,620 --> 00:16:30,370
All my life, I kept changing schools.

322
00:16:30,540 --> 00:16:32,000
I won't let you go further.

323
00:16:32,080 --> 00:16:33,120
Watch out!

324
00:16:34,260 --> 00:16:39,120
The interesting thing is, Furano, Miwa, and Nankatsu...

325
00:16:39,380 --> 00:16:43,380
...were all schools strong in football.

326
00:16:44,470 --> 00:16:49,470
My father must have chosen those schools.

327
00:16:50,220 --> 00:16:52,350
I finally understand.

328
00:16:52,850 --> 00:16:54,640
Thank you, Dad.

329
00:16:55,140 --> 00:16:58,520
I had to say goodbye to many friends.

330
00:16:58,810 --> 00:17:01,940
But the soccer ball was always there...

331
00:17:02,400 --> 00:17:06,200
The soccer ball was always with me.

332
00:17:06,280 --> 00:17:10,200
The soccer ball will remain my friend forever.

333
00:17:10,950 --> 00:17:14,290
Misaki approaches the penalty area.

334
00:17:14,580 --> 00:17:16,040
Well done, Misaki.

335
00:17:16,370 --> 00:17:18,040
I won't let you cross.

336
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:19,040
Taro!

337
00:17:19,670 --> 00:17:22,300
Germany tackles without fear of committing a foul.

338
00:17:23,550 --> 00:17:25,420
I leave the rest to you.

339
00:17:25,510 --> 00:17:28,930
Oh, the tackle came to Misaki's right foot.

340
00:17:29,010 --> 00:17:31,550
But he still managed to cross.

341
00:17:31,800 --> 00:17:32,810
Great.

342
00:17:33,060 --> 00:17:38,810
And here, none other than Japan's best young forward, Kojiro Hyuga, is running.

343
00:17:39,100 --> 00:17:41,060
Hurry, stop him! Don't let him shoot!

344
00:17:41,230 --> 00:17:43,650
Germany fiercely goes to block.

345
00:17:43,730 --> 00:17:46,400
Oh, but the ball goes through! Hyuga let it go!

346
00:17:46,490 --> 00:17:47,320
What!?

347
00:17:48,030 --> 00:17:51,320
We vowed together, our dream is to be number one in the world...

348
00:17:51,990 --> 00:17:53,790
Now it's your turn, captain.

349
00:17:54,290 --> 00:17:56,120
Captain Tsubasa!

350
00:17:56,660 --> 00:17:59,830
Tsubasa has reached the front of the goal.

351
00:18:00,830 --> 00:18:04,840
Tsubasa jumps at the same time as Misaki's cross.

352
00:18:05,170 --> 00:18:08,340
And takes an unmarked flying scissor kick!

353
00:18:08,590 --> 00:18:09,590
I won't allow it!

354
00:18:10,050 --> 00:18:14,140
Oh, but Schneider jumps at the same time.

355
00:18:14,220 --> 00:18:16,600
And a tremendous tackle at the critical moment!

356
00:18:16,680 --> 00:18:20,020
Tsubasa, carrying Japan's dream with a flying scissor...

357
00:18:20,100 --> 00:18:22,860
...was stopped by a flying scissor!

358
00:18:23,230 --> 00:18:24,360
Schneider!

359
00:18:26,190 --> 00:18:30,110
2-2 draw! Are we going to extra time?

360
00:18:30,410 --> 00:18:32,490
Not yet. I don't give up.

361
00:18:32,990 --> 00:18:35,990
I just blocked it, I still need to clear it.

362
00:18:36,540 --> 00:18:38,500
The ball still hasn't gone out of play.

363
00:18:38,870 --> 00:18:42,500
Tsubasa managed to land unsteadily.

364
00:18:42,920 --> 00:18:45,000
Schneider is also on his feet.

365
00:18:45,380 --> 00:18:48,420
The great rivals jump for the ball once again.

366
00:18:52,050 --> 00:18:55,470
Tsubasa or Schneider? Who is faster?

367
00:18:55,560 --> 00:18:56,390
Tsubasa!

368
00:18:56,810 --> 00:18:58,140
Schneider!

369
00:19:01,390 --> 00:19:05,900
Tsubasa! He was a moment faster.

370
00:19:06,230 --> 00:19:07,360
I'll catch it!

371
00:19:08,320 --> 00:19:10,650
Müller can't reach it.

372
00:19:10,780 --> 00:19:13,660
But it's too high! It's going out!

373
00:19:14,030 --> 00:19:15,410
Oh, did he miss?

374
00:19:17,450 --> 00:19:18,540
What!?

375
00:19:19,410 --> 00:19:21,910
No, this is a Drive Shot!

376
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:24,920
He not only struck the ball a moment before Schneider...

377
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:28,050
...he also put spin on it.

378
00:19:28,130 --> 00:19:33,680
This is the shot of the genius footballer Ozora Tsubasa, the Flying Scissor Drive.

379
00:19:36,100 --> 00:19:37,930
The referee puts the whistle to his mouth.

380
00:19:38,220 --> 00:19:42,940
Tsubasa goes to strike the spinning ball!

381
00:19:50,280 --> 00:19:52,570
Tsubasa jumps!

382
00:19:53,070 --> 00:19:54,570
This...

383
00:19:57,700 --> 00:19:59,240
Final shot!

384
00:19:59,330 --> 00:20:03,080
Tsubasa executes a ground-level overhead kick!

385
00:20:03,250 --> 00:20:04,080
I got it!

386
00:20:04,170 --> 00:20:08,840
But Germany's goalkeeper Müller reacts and dives in its direction.

387
00:20:10,920 --> 00:20:11,760
What!?

388
00:20:11,840 --> 00:20:15,340
The ball rises and goes into the air!

389
00:20:17,680 --> 00:20:19,890
It's- It's in the goal!

390
00:20:21,140 --> 00:20:24,100
And the final whistle declares the end of the game.

391
00:20:24,190 --> 00:20:28,360
The Japanese youth win! They did it!

392
00:20:28,440 --> 00:20:32,490
Japan has become the world champion!

393
00:20:35,910 --> 00:20:37,530
We did it!

394
00:20:38,160 --> 00:20:39,620
We won.

395
00:20:40,080 --> 00:20:41,620
We won.

396
00:20:42,120 --> 00:20:43,620
Tsubasa.

397
00:20:46,210 --> 00:20:47,630
Number one in the world.

398
00:20:50,130 --> 00:20:51,630
Yes!

399
00:20:53,880 --> 00:20:55,380
Tsubasa.

400
00:20:55,720 --> 00:20:56,880
We did it.

401
00:20:57,840 --> 00:21:01,140
We did it! We won!

402
00:21:01,390 --> 00:21:02,470
We won!

403
00:21:02,560 --> 00:21:03,810
We are the champions!

404
00:21:03,890 --> 00:21:05,520
We did it!

405
00:21:05,600 --> 00:21:07,190
Japan won!

406
00:21:07,270 --> 00:21:08,400
Tsubasa.

407
00:21:09,690 --> 00:21:10,820
Guys.

408
00:21:10,900 --> 00:21:13,030
Japan won!

409
00:21:19,530 --> 00:21:21,910
Hurray, hurray, hurray!

410
00:21:23,870 --> 00:21:25,290
Matsuyama.

411
00:21:25,960 --> 00:21:31,750
The entire Japan team runs toward their champion, captain Tsubasa.

412
00:21:31,880 --> 00:21:34,170
Even the substitutes.

413
00:21:34,460 --> 00:21:36,170
Your shot was great, Tsubasa.

414
00:21:36,260 --> 00:21:38,430
I knew you would finish it.

415
00:21:38,800 --> 00:21:41,390
See? I told you.

416
00:21:41,470 --> 00:21:45,180
Tsubasa always finds a way, you little rascal!

417
00:21:45,680 --> 00:21:46,560
Ishizaki.

418
00:21:46,640 --> 00:21:47,690
Ishizaki.

419
00:21:48,230 --> 00:21:50,560
No, it was thanks to you all.

420
00:21:50,650 --> 00:21:53,190
We succeeded thanks to your hard work.

421
00:21:53,690 --> 00:21:55,690
We won!

422
00:21:58,150 --> 00:22:01,660
We became number one, and our dream has come true.

423
00:22:01,910 --> 00:22:07,120
Thank God. I'm so happy to be a footballer.

424
00:24:45,740 --> 00:24:49,990
Next Episode
A Vow to the Sky